.TH SH-SYNTH 1
.SH NAME
synth \- shell script interface to sequencer(2)'s command language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B load synth

.B ${synth
.B new
.B }
.br
.B synth
.I id
.B noteon
.I voice midinote
.br
.B synth
.I id
.B noteoff
.I voice
.br
.B synth
.I id
.B play
.I file
.br
.B synth
.I id
.B stop
.br
.B synth del
.I id...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Synth
is a loadable module for
.IR sh (1)
giving shell scripts direct access to
.IR sequencer (2)'s
own
.B Session
command language \(em playing notes and SKINI scores through the CSP
synthesizer from a script, without a compiled Limbo program.
.PP
.B ${synth new}
allocates a handle wrapping a fresh
.IR sequencer (2)
.B Session
(one master
.BR Inst ),
and yields it.
.BR Noteon ,
.BR noteoff ,
.BR play ,
and
.B stop
each call
.IR sequencer (2)'s
own
.B Session.cmd
unchanged; see
.IR sequencer (2)
for what each verb means, including why
.B play
returns immediately rather than blocking until the score finishes,
and why a second
.B play
while one is already running is an error.
.B Del
frees one or more handles \(em it only removes the shell's own
bookkeeping, the same as
.IR sh-pde (1)'s
own
.BR del ;
the session's underlying voice processes are long-lived by design (see
.IR sequencer (2))
and are not torn down by it.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
	load synth
	id := ${synth new}
	synth $id noteon 0 60
	synth $id noteoff 0
	synth $id play /appl/lib/bachtest.ski
	synth $id stop
	synth del $id
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/sh/synth.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR sequencer (2),
.IR playski (1),
.IR sh (1),
.IR sh-pde (1)
